  "title": "Hiragana 2: ら to ん, voiced sounds, combinations",
  "note": "゛ voices a sound: か ka → が ga, さ → ざ, た → だ, は → ば; ゜ gives p: ぱ pa. A small ゃ ゅ ょ joins the sign before it (きゃ kya), a small っ doubles the next consonant (きって kitte), and long vowels take a macron (がっこう gakkō). As particles, は is read wa, へ e and を o.",
